// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6540 Sigma: PavinLoader fake-driver MSI campaign (MSBuild from %LOCALAPPDATA%, MSBUILDENABLEALLPROPERTYFUNCTIONS, fake dllhost/taskhostw tasks, m
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6540
// Pull request author: fotedev
// Change: new rule
// Title: Scheduled Task Files Masquerading as System Binaries (dllhost/taskhostw)
// Sigma ID: d5ba62a1-5139-47f9-992d-a93cdf3f5fb2
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: fotedev
// Date: 2026-10-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1053.005
// Description: Detects creation (or modification) of scheduled task files named "dllhost" or "taskhostw" under
//   C:\Windows\System32\Tasks - names masquerading as the legitimate system binaries dllhost.exe /
//   taskhostw.exe. Observed PavinLoader.BAT persistence dropped such task files. Note that the Task
//   Scheduler service (svchost.exe) writes task XML natively for all task-creation APIs, so the
//   writer process does not distinguish legitimate from malicious creation here; the masquerading
//   name is the signal.
// False positives:
//   - Administrative tooling or configuration management that legitimately registers tasks with these exact names (uncommon; the names impersonate system binaries)
// References:
//   - https://github.com/fotedev/pavinloader-easeus-campaign
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/005/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6ead36c4ad43fd558f6614e9debb235df9de2d40/rules/windows/file_event/file_event_win_schtask_files_dllhost_taskhostw.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\Windows\\System32\\Tasks\\dllhost" or FolderPath endswith "\\Windows\\System32\\Tasks\\taskhostw"
